# Implementation Plan (Revised): Visual Engine Stability

Previous attempts to fix the matrix rendering and 3D canvas failed because:
1.  **Scanner Logic Error**: The brace-matching scanner was prematurely matching `}}` tags within `\end{pmatrix}}}` environments.
2.  **3D Initialization Race**: MathBox was attempting texture creation (leading to 'LOD' errors) before the DOM container had a non-zero size.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> - I am rewriting the `EquationParser.ts` scanner to prioritize `{{ }}` tag identification over single `{ }` math braces.
> - I will delay the 3D MathBox context creation until the DOM element has stabilized its dimensions.

## Proposed Changes

### [Component Name] Engine Overhaul

#### [MODIFY] [EquationParser.ts](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/MathLessonVisualiser/src/engine/EquationParser.ts) [REVISION]
- Rewrite `segmentEquation` to handle nested braces by scanning for `{{`, then `|`, then finding the correct `}}`.
- Fix the `braceLevel` logic to skip over single `{` and `}` that are part of the LaTeX string without confusing them with the `{{` and `}}` markers.

#### [MODIFY] [EquationRenderer.tsx](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/MathLessonVisualiser/src/renderers/EquationRenderer.tsx)
- Ensure segmented LaTeX terms are rendered as math-mode strings (wrapped in `$ ... $` if needed or using `\\displaystyle`).
- Add a safety check to ensure terms aren't empty before rendering.

#### [MODIFY] [Canvas3DRenderer.tsx](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/MathLessonVisualiser/src/renderers/Canvas3DRenderer.tsx) [REVISION]
- Change `initMathBox` to check `clientWidth > 0` before proceeding.
- Move the `view.axis()` call to be protected by a check that avoids texture allocation until specifically requested.
- Ensure only essential 3D objects are rendered to minimize WebGL context stress.

